        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "Obligations and the tests that cover them:\n\n1. **Workspace Rustdoc is generated during preprocessing, including on a first build in a fresh checkout.**\n   - `tests/rustdocs.rs#fn[rustdocs_workspace_build_generates_and_refreshes_the_import]` starts from a fresh temporary project with no `target` directory. It sets `build-workspace = true` and calls `habeas::rustdocs::preprocess`.\n   - It asserts that `fn.first.html` is imported for the root crate and that `member/fn.marker.html` is imported for a workspace member.\n   - It asserts that an excluded dependency is not imported.\n   - It asserts that a later source change produces `fn.second.html`, so generation runs on each build.\n   - It asserts the failure paths: a `path` that doesn't end in `doc`, a failed `cargo doc` (with no `Cargo.lock` created), and a broken source file that keeps the previous import.\n   - `mdbook build` and `mdbook serve` both run the same preprocessor, and the text doesn't distinguish them. Testing the preprocessor entry point therefore covers both.\n\n2. **The book and the generated Rustdoc ship in the same GitHub Pages deployment.**\n   - `tests/rustdocs.rs#fn[rustdocs_ci_publishes_the_book_with_workspace_generation_enabled]` parses `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. It asserts that the `mdbook build` step comes before `actions/upload-pages-artifact@v4`, and that the uploaded path is `book`.\n   - It asserts that `book.toml` sets `build-workspace = true`, `crate = \"trust_but_verify\"` and `path = \"target/doc\"`. It also asserts the `output.habeas` command.\n   - The imported site is placed under the book output. That behavior belongs to `requirements.index.rustdocs`, which the first test also covers. Together these checks tie the single uploaded `book` artifact to the generated Rustdoc.\n\n3. **The appendix has a \"Rustdocs\" entry that opens the `trust_but_verify` documentation.**\n   - The CI test asserts that `md/SUMMARY.md` has `[Rustdocs](./rustdocs.md)` after `# Appendix`.\n   - It asserts that `md/rustdocs.md` contains exactly the standalone `:::{rustdocs}` / `:::` directive.\n   - It asserts that the configured crate is `trust_but_verify`.\n\nThe cited `requirements.integration.ci` and `requirements.index.rustdocs` are context only, and I did not reassess their tests. Both tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unmarked relevant test and no unacknowledged gap."
      }
